# Theory of Computation - JFLAP Programs

## Problem 1

### Aim
To construct a Finite Automaton using JFLAP.

### Tool Used
JFLAP

### Alphabet
{a}

### States
- q0 – Initial state
- q1 – Final state
- q2 – Reject state

### Transitions
- q0 --a--> q1
- q1 --a--> q2
- q2 --a--> q2

### Sample Inputs

| Input | Result |
|---|---|
| a | Accept |
| aa | Reject |
| aaa | Reject |
| aaaa | Reject |

### Output
The automaton accepts `a` and rejects strings containing two or more `a` symbols.
